      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Close the bean",
      "summary": "The closing half of every bean's life: end it in a state that says why.",
      "description": "The closing half of every bean's life: end it in a state that says why. Done work is completed and archived; unwanted work is scrapped with its reasons — never deleted — and archived; blocked work records what it waits on and goes back to `todo` for whoever can act. Called, never run on its own, straight before an end event of a process that called Process_BeanOpen.\n\nA bean is never deleted. A scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end; a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/bean-close.bpmn",
